Z||000000||TxFieros||07-06-2001||04:29 PM||||I've been looking everywhere for someone able to give me some insight as to wheels that will fit my Fiero just right.  I don't trust shops, so I won't take their word for it.<P>I'm looking at putting 17's on my Formula, but I don't went them to stick out more than they do now, and I don't want them further in than they are now.  If I am not mistaken, aren't the fronts 6.0 inch wide wheels, and the backs 6.5?  Also, just from looking and the front to back wheels you can tell the offset is different.  The back wheels look great there, but if you stick them up front the car looks terrible with the tires sticking so far out, and the fronts on the back are placed inward which looks geeky.<P>I suppose the rears on the front look much more extreme than they would with the 205's because 225 60's are on those rims.<P>The wheels I'm looking at are 17x7's which means that the backspacing and offset will probably be a bit different than stock.<P>Does anyone know what specs. a 17x7 wheel should have to retain that stock offset look? Not too far in and not too far out.<P>Carlos<BR>'88 Formula 5-speed with many tweaks.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrgone||07-06-2001||04:37 PM||||welcome to the forum, <P>alot of the members have sweet rims on their car like the ones you described. help on this topic should be no problem.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_9.jpg">   <BR><B>86.5 2m4 5speed turd 241,000kms</B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||qwikgta||07-07-2001||12:17 AM||||Carlos,  I too have a 88 and I understand your feelings.  I had 87 GT rims on mine and the front stuck out about an inch on each side because the offset was the same on the front and back rims unlike the 88 rims. (you already know this).  I used the search function on the forum and looked for info on rims.  Many threads have been done on this subject over the last few months and it pops up every month or so too.  Many fourm members have 17" on their Fieros.  I went with 16" Beretta GTZ rims and 205/225 rubber, its not that bad and gives me room to lower it about 2" which is a future project.<P>Good luck<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||DecadenceR||07-07-2001||01:15 AM||||From what i've read, a 225/45R17 would fit stock pretty well. And I believe you ned a 35mm offest, and I don't remember the bolt pattern spacing. But, I could be wrong because I had notes and can't seem to find them. There are a few people here that have 17's, they can help you.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SigPic.jpg">  <BR>AIM - DecadenceR<BR>"For though I cannot fly, I'm not content to crawl..."||||reg||1
